The establishment of the vulnerability is intrinsic to the code provided and does not rely on the states or behaviors of other external contracts aside from the known dependency `_stUsdc` (specified in the function call `_stUsdc.sharesByUsd(1 ether)`). The vulnerability exists purely due to the incorrect unit assumption within the provided code snippet and does not depend on any external calls or states affecting this calculation. Thus, resolving this vulnerability would only require rectifying the unit conversion within the same function without needing insights or alterations into other unknown contracts' code within the project itself.

