The exploitation of the `sharesOf` function does not rely on the code of other unknown or unprovided contracts within the project, nor does it depend on external calls or contract states. The vulnerability exists solely due to the ability of any external entity to query the shares associated with any account directly from this function.

The attack leverages publicly accessible information from the `sharesOf` function itself without requiring interactions with any other contracts or dependencies on additional functionalities. Thus, the establishment of this vulnerability operates independently of other in-project contract interactions or external dependencies.

